steps.instructions:
Add sample TechPath course data to your `rag_bot.py` file. This simulates loading real documents:

```python
from langchain_core.documents import Document
from langchain.text_splitter import RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter

# Sample documents about TechPath Institute
documents = [
    Document(
        page_content="TechPath Institute is located in Bhopal, near MP Nagar Zone-II. The campus has modern computer labs and high-speed internet. Online batches are available for students in Delhi, Pune, and Indore.",
        metadata={"source": "about.txt"}
    ),
    Document(
        page_content="Python Full Stack course: Duration 6 months, Fee Rs 45,000 including GST. Classes Monday to Friday, 10 AM to 1 PM. Maximum 20 students per batch. No prior programming experience needed.",
        metadata={"source": "courses.txt"}
    ),
    Document(
        page_content="AI/ML course: Duration 4 months, Fee Rs 35,000 including GST. Covers Machine Learning, Deep Learning, NLP. Weekend batch available Saturday-Sunday 10 AM to 2 PM.",
        metadata={"source": "courses.txt"}
    ),
    Document(
        page_content="Placement support: 85% placement rate within 3 months. Average package Rs 4-6 LPA. Top recruiters include TCS, Infosys, Wipro, HCL. Resume building and mock interviews provided.",
        metadata={"source": "placements.txt"}
    ),
    Document(
        page_content="Scholarships: Early bird discount Rs 5,000 off. Women in Tech scholarship 15% fee waiver. Sibling discount 10% off. 3-month and 6-month no-cost EMI available.",
        metadata={"source": "fees.txt"}
    ),
    Document(
        page_content="Contact TechPath: Email info@techpath.biz, Phone +91 98765 43210. Office hours Monday to Saturday 9 AM to 6 PM. Admission process: Online form then counseling call then fee payment.",
        metadata={"source": "contact.txt"}
    ),
]

# Split documents into smaller chunks
splitter = RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(chunk_size=300, chunk_overlap=30)
chunks = splitter.split_documents(documents)

print(f"Original documents: {len(documents)}")
print(f"After splitting: {len(chunks)} chunks")
for i, chunk in enumerate(chunks):
    print(f"  Chunk {i+1} ({len(chunk.page_content)} chars, source: {chunk.metadata['source']})")
```

Run the file. You should see the chunks listed with their sizes and sources.
